      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "infinitivo como etiqueta de acción",
      "questionEn": "Why can a Spanish diagram label an action with a verb that has not changed for a person?",
      "answerEn": "Use the verb's dictionary form as a compact label for an action, event, or step.",
      "noteEn": "The dictionary form is called the infinitive and ends in -ar, -er, or -ir. It does not identify a person or time. Diagrams, timelines, checklists, recipe steps, and buttons can use it to name an action without building a full command.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Preparar los ingredientes.",
        "en": "Prepare the ingredients."
      },
      "tags": ["grammar", "infinitives", "instructions", "A2"]
    },
